package com.bqsqwad.heartbreakhealer.feature.entertainment

internal object StoryLibraryBatch70 {
    val stories = listOf(
        StorySeries(
            id = "the_rooftop_seed_library",
            title = "The Rooftop Seed Library",
            tagline = "A forgotten packet of seeds helps neighbours rebuild a shared garden.",
            parts = listOf(
                StoryPart(1, "The Locked Rooftop", listOf("The apartment building had a rooftop garden, but its gate had been locked for so long that most residents assumed it was unsafe. When Kosi moved into the top floor, she noticed green leaves pushing through a crack beside the stairwell door.", "Her neighbour Arun said the garden had once been cared for by residents from every floor. A disagreement about water bills had ended the project, and the key was supposedly lost.", "Kosi found a small envelope taped behind the noticeboard. Inside were three seed packets and a note: 'A garden begins when someone shares the first seed.'")),
                StoryPart(2, "The Caretaker's Drawer", listOf("The building caretaker, Mr Nwosu, searched his drawer of old keys. He remembered the rooftop garden but said the lock had been changed after a storm damaged the gate.", "He found a maintenance record showing that the gate was sound and the roof had been inspected. The garden had closed because nobody could agree on how to organise it, not because the space was dangerous.", "Kosi asked whether the residents could discuss reopening it. Mr Nwosu agreed to bring the inspection record to the next building meeting.")),
                StoryPart(3, "Seeds with No Labels", listOf("The seed packets had no labels, only small drawings: a sun, a bowl, and a blue bird. Kosi took them to her science teacher, who explained that old seeds could be difficult to identify without careful testing.", "They decided not to plant unknown seeds immediately. Instead, they asked a local gardening group to help identify them and check whether they were suitable for containers.", "The group recognised one packet as a variety of leafy vegetable, but the other two needed more research. Kosi wrote the names in pencil so the labels could be corrected if new evidence appeared.")),
                StoryPart(4, "The Meeting on Floor Five", listOf("At the building meeting, residents raised the old argument about water costs. Some wanted the garden reopened, while others worried that a few volunteers would end up doing all the work.", "Arun suggested a rota with small tasks: checking soil, collecting rainwater where permitted, cleaning shared tools, and reporting problems. The residents agreed that nobody should be expected to contribute more than they could manage.", "They also decided that the garden would grow a few useful plants rather than become a competition for the prettiest rooftop. Kosi volunteered to keep the rota visible and easy to change.")),
                StoryPart(5, "The Blue Bird Packet", listOf("A retired teacher named Mrs Bello recognised the blue bird drawing. She had helped start the garden and used the symbol to mark seeds donated by a school gardening club.", "She remembered that the packet contained a flowering plant chosen to attract pollinators. The school still had a copy of the original planting guide, including advice about container depth and sunlight.", "Mrs Bello offered to help the residents plan the layout, but she insisted that they leave space for people to sit and enjoy the roof without having to garden.")),
                StoryPart(6, "A Place for Everyone", listOf("The residents measured the rooftop and marked a clear walking route. They placed containers where the inspection report said the surface could support them and kept the doorway and emergency access unobstructed.", "A neighbour who used a mobility aid suggested wider gaps between the planters and a table at a reachable height. The group adjusted the design before buying anything.", "Kosi noticed that the best plan was not the one with the most plants. It was the one that allowed the greatest number of neighbours to use the space comfortably.")),
                StoryPart(7, "The First Planting", listOf("On planting day, the gardening group brought labelled containers and fresh soil. The residents planted only the identified seeds and kept the uncertain packets aside until they could be checked properly.", "Children made weather labels, adults assembled a simple watering rota, and Mr Nwosu installed a notice explaining how to report maintenance concerns.", "Arun planted the first leafy vegetables beside Mrs Bello's flowers. The rooftop looked modest, but the residents agreed it was better to begin carefully than to promise more than they could maintain.")),
                StoryPart(8, "The Week Without Rain", listOf("A dry week tested the rota. Two volunteers were away, and one container began to look tired. Instead of blaming anyone, the residents reviewed the schedule and asked for backup volunteers.", "They learned that the building's approved water-saving system could collect rain when it returned, but they would still need a reliable plan during dry periods. The caretaker helped them set a reasonable limit for water use.", "Kosi updated the rota with a shared contact list and a reminder that residents could swap duties. The garden survived the week, and the group became more organised.")),
                StoryPart(9, "The Seed Exchange", listOf("When the first vegetables were ready, the residents held a small seed and recipe exchange. Mrs Bello brought planting notes, Arun shared a family recipe, and children displayed drawings of the rooftop birds.", "The two unidentified packets were finally checked by the gardening group. One was too old to use, while the other contained a suitable herb. The residents recorded the result rather than planting it without certainty.", "A neighbouring building asked how they had reopened the space. Kosi shared the rota, accessibility notes, and inspection checklist, explaining that each building would need its own safety review.")),
                StoryPart(10, "A Garden Kept Together", listOf("By the end of the season, the rooftop held vegetables, flowers, a shaded table, and a small cabinet for labelled seeds. The residents kept the original envelope in a display frame beside the entrance.", "They wrote a new note beneath it: 'Share the work as carefully as you share the seeds.' The garden had no single owner, and its success depended on clear agreements and room for people to participate in different ways.", "Kosi looked across the rooftops and saw other small green spaces appearing. The old garden had not returned exactly as it was. It had become something more thoughtful: a place built from lessons, cooperation, and a promise that nobody had to tend it alone.")
                )
            )
        )
    )
}
